  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "An unresolved issue is the extent to which epistasis is involved in inbreeding depression. As noted above, a nonlinear relationship between the mean phenotype and the inbreeding coefficient is an indicator of the presence of epistasis involving dominance effects. Least-squares quadratic regressions are frequently performed to test for such nonlinearities, but these are saddled with all of the statistical problems discussed above, most notably the extreme nonindependence of data at high levels of f, precisely where nonlinearities are most likely to show up.",
      "source_page": 283,
      "printed_page": 263,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter10:p017:b3",
        "Genetics_chapter10:p017:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        57.0,
        549.0,
        1018.0,
        788.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        283
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
