    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Although it can only detect epistatic effects involving dominance, this test is one of the only ways that we currently have to quantify directional epistasis within populations, short of employing molecular markers. Willis (1993) used a very similar approach to test for epistasis for life-history characters in the monkey flower (Mimulus guttatus). Although he did not correct for line loss, he found very little evidence for epistasis.",
